    "result_text": "Done. I agreed with both findings and refactored accordingly.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **Reverted `SaveOwner`** back to its persistence-only form. It's shared by both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, so the audit logic there would have fired on every update too \u2014 a behavioral leak beyond the spec's \"on successful create\" scope, and a responsibility smell on a reused step.\n\n2. **Added `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 a dedicated single-responsibility step holding its own `AUDIT` logger and reading `@Val Owner`, matching the step-per-concern idiom the rest of the package follows (`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, `CountOwnerNamesakes`, etc.).\n\n3. **Wired `audit` into `owners.POST.yml` only**, between `save` and `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps. The PUT pipeline is untouched, so audit emission is now scoped to the create path.\n\n## Verification\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The AUDIT line still carries all three values from the dedicated step:\n\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-05\n```",
